    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d394">

                <pb facs="0485" n="373" xml:id="pg373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 M 832/26: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-04T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4, 1919,
                                12 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 5, 3:32
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2413. For Polk.</p>
                <p>Your 2139, May 29, 4 p.m.<anchor n="97" xml:id="d394-f1"/> The President states
                    that since it does not appear that Mr. Morris has even started for Omsk, no advantage can be derived
                    from his going at all and accordingly the original instructions to proceed to
                    Omsk should be cancelled.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
